  "notes": "{奏|かな}でる is a transitive verb with a literary, poetic nuance.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: [instrument]で + [music/melody]を{奏|かな}でる\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- メロディーを{奏|かな}でる (play a melody)\n- {曲|きょく}を{奏|かな}でる (play a piece)\n- ハーモニーを{奏|かな}でる (produce a harmony)\n- {音色|ねいろ}を{奏|かな}でる (produce a tone)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {弾|ひ}く: the everyday word for playing piano, guitar, and other stringed/keyboard instruments\n- {吹|ふ}く: for wind instruments\n- {奏|かな}でる: more literary and elegant; used for poetic or formal descriptions of music-making, and can extend figuratively to natural sounds",
